m that this cosmos  is ruled by evil forces that look like  animals that after death our souls must  ascend past these powers to get to  heaven and that you need to know certain  prayers and passwords to get by them  here we see again that these early  traditions about Mary are not  necessarily fully Orthodox shortly  before Mary is to die all the Apostles  gathered to where she lives in Jerusalem  because the Apostles are scattered all  over the world preaching the gospel they  must be transported there miraculously  on clouds after prayers and discussion  it's time for Mary to die she dresses in  special garments and lies down  Christ arrives with many angels and he  takes Mary's soul and gives it to  Michael the Archangel Mary's soul is  said to be a perfect form but its body  was both male and female and  nevertheless one being similar to every  body and seven times white that is its  supremely white as both male and female  and yet one and completely white Mary's  soul represents humanity without sin  humanity before the fall of Adam and Eve  completely one both male and female and  entirely pure the apostles prepare  Mary's body for burial and they place it  on a stretcher and carry it in a in a  procession to her tomb the Jews tried to  attack the funeral present procession  kill the Apostles and burn Mary's body  angels protect the procession from the  attacking Jews but one of the Jewish  priests is able to touch the stretcher  when he does his hands become severed  from his arms and they hang from the  stretcher until Peter heals him a few  days after Mary's body is buried Christ  returns and takes her body he reunites  it with her soul and places Mary near  the Tree of Life in paradise and so  Mary's body and soul are both assumed  into paradise but the book of Mary's  repose does not stop there Mary and the  Apostles are then permitted to see the  sufferings of sinners in hell the damned  people cry out to Mary Mary  we deceit you Mary light and the mother  of light Mary life and the mother of the  Apostles Mary golden lamp you who carry  every righteous lamp Mary our master and  the mother of our master Mary our queen  seats your son to give us a little rest  the apostle  scorn this request why didn't the Damned  listen to them when they were alive but  Jesus decides to give the damned three  hours of relief from their sufferings  every Sunday because of the tears of  Michael the Apostles and his mother Mary  here we see the idea that Mary can  intercede for sinful human beings and  pure procure from her son relief for  those who suffer the book concludes with  the Apostles returning to earth and Mary  seated on a throne in paradise she truly  is as she was acclaimed a queen possibly  this author has identified Mary with the  Queen like woman who appears in the book  of Revelation as the mother of a special  child in this remarkable apocryphal text  from the 3rd century we find key  elements of how Christian saw Mary in  late antiquity she has special esoteric  knowledge of mysteries which Christ has  shared with her her soul and body are  pure and spotless she therefore does not  die as other people do instead she lies  down and sleeps at God's command and her  soul and body are taken to paradise and  sinful human beings can ask her to  intercede in their behalf with Christ  some of these elements appear also in  the six books Dormition apocryphon from  the 4th century it gets its name because  it's divided into six parts called books  like the book of Mary's repose the six  books was written in Greek but the  original Greek does not survive in this  case we have a serious serious Latian in  multiple manuscripts from the 5th and  6th centuries the six books is the  earliest of a number of narratives about  Mary's Dormition that center around  Bethlehem and Jerusalem and it's likely  that it reflects the growing piety  directed towards Mary that developed in  the Holy Land during the fourth century  the six books 