ix books  Dormition apocryphon shows clearly that  some Christians are now venerating Mary  with scheduled festival days the text  instructs its readers to honor Mary on  certain days and it associates Mary  especially with agricultural prosperity  as well as healings the book includes  the offering of bread in the name of the  Virgin this last point is especially  significant because in the late 300s a  Christian bishop named epifanio's based  on the island of Cyprus wrote about  Christians who he said made bread  offerings to the Virgin Mary he called  these Christians  Koller idioms and he criticized their  veneration of Mary as inappropriate in  the case of a human being he accused  them of worshipping Mary as if she were  God but epifanio's did not like much of  what Christians around him were doing  especially the emerging cult of the  Saints during the 4th century Christians  developed a set of practices in which  they would communicate with and have  fellowship with deceased saints  especially the apostles and martyrs  Christians would honor their remains or  relics worship at their tombs and ask  them to intercede with God in their  behalf veneration of Mary which we see  in the six books Dormition apocryphon  was part of this growing trend Mary  however held a special place among the  Saints for she had given birth to the  Son of God himself and so she was known  in Greek as the Theotokos the one who  gave birth to go  or the mother of God as such her body  was holy and pure and so it did not die  normally but went straight to paradise  likewise Mary was particularly well  suited to petition her son Christ in  behalf of sinful or sick human beings in  the 420s mist aureus the bishop of the  imperial capital of Constantinople  denied that Mary should be called the  mother of God God can't be born he  argued he has no mother instead Mary  gave birth to the human Jesus with whom  the Son of God  United other bishops had problems with  mysterious teachings for